/// <summary>
/// How the current link speed/duplex was decided. PARALLEL_DETECTED is the
/// duplex-mismatch smoking gun: it means the link partner did not transmit
/// FLP bursts, so the PHY had to detect speed only and (per IEEE 802.3)
/// pick half-duplex. If the partner is actually configured full-duplex,
/// every collision they see is "late" and TCP loses retransmits.
/// </summary>
